{
  "dom_id": "step-q182010",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Complete the following reasoning about the set $S=(4,\\infty ):$\n\nThe value $100$ is not the maximum of the set $S$ because {{field-1}} and yet {{field-2}}.",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that ${x}_{max}$ is the maximum of a set $S$ if \n\n- ${x}_{max}\\in S,$ and\n\n- $x\\le {x}_{max}$ for all $x\\in S.$\n\nIn our case, the value $100$ is not the maximum of the set $S$ because, for example, $101\\in S$ and yet $101>100.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
